      "date": "2026-07-27 19:57:46.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nExperimental feature testing in progress, please pay attention to the comments\n\nThe move itself looks correct: init_test_env() exports TMP (test-framework.sh, via cfg/$NAME.sh and `export TMP=${TMP:-$ROOT/tmp}`) before the new assignment site, and nothing between the old and new positions reads LREPL_LOG. One comment on the commit message. Separately, performance-sanity.sh still has the same early-$TMP pattern (LOG=${LOG:-\"$TMP/${TESTNAME}.log\"} above init_test_env) if you want to sweep it in a follow-on patch.",
